From: Mario Geiger <geiger.mario@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] P2P: CHECKPRESENT does not report content locked for removal

Two repositories that each hold a copy of a key, and are each other's P2P
remotes, can both drop the key at the same time and leave no copy, even with
numcopies = mincopies = 2.

Command/Drop.hs performLocal (line 131) takes the content's removal lock,
then verifyEnoughCopiesToDrop (Annex/NumCopies.hs, line 255) asks each remote
to LOCKCONTENT. The other side's lock fails, because that side holds its own
removal lock, so the drop falls back to CHECKPRESENT and counts a
RecentlyVerifiedCopy (line 279). With a removal lock held, safeDropAnalysis
(Types/NumCopies.hs, line 196) accepts copies of any kind, because the lock
"will prevent other git repos that are concurrently dropping from using the
local copy as a VerifiedCopy".

Over a local path that holds: checklocal in Remote/Git.hs (line 490) uses
inAnnexSafe, which reports content locked for removal as not present. Over
P2P it does not: the server answers CHECKPRESENT (P2P/Protocol.hs, line 645)
through CheckContentPresent, which P2P/Annex.hs (line 129) runs with inAnnex,
ignoring the lock. So each side counts the other's copy and both drop.

Run CheckContentPresent with inAnnexSafe, as checklocal does, treating
content locked for removal as not present. CheckContentPresent also decides
ALREADY-HAVE for PUT and DATA-PRESENT (P2P/Protocol.hs, lines 686 and 696);
there too, content that is being removed is better not claimed.

Reproducer: lab/git-annex/ga-e23-p2p-drop.py in
https://github.com/mariogeiger/pigeon (branch v2), which races two drops at a
barrier, over P2P and over a local path.
---
 P2P/Annex.hs | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/P2P/Annex.hs
+++ b/P2P/Annex.hs
@@ -127,7 +127,12 @@
 			Left e -> return $ Left $ ProtoFailureException e
 			Right () -> runner next
 	CheckContentPresent k next -> do
-		v <- tryNonAsync $ inAnnex k
+		-- Content that is locked for removal is in the process of
+		-- being dropped, so it is not reported as present. Otherwise
+		-- two repositories that drop the same key at the same time
+		-- could each count the other's copy and both drop it. This
+		-- is the same check that Remote.Git uses for a local remote.
+		v <- tryNonAsync $ fromMaybe False <$> inAnnexSafe k
 		case v of
 			Left e -> return $ Left $ ProtoFailureException e
 			Right result -> runner (next result)
